+\begin{lemma}
+\label{lemma-spec-homeomorphism-onto-image-units}
+\begin{reference}
+\cite[Corollary 1.2.4]{EGA1}
+\end{reference}
+Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Assume that every $g \in S$
+can be written as $g = u\varphi(f)$ for some $f \in R$ and some
+unit $u \in S$. Then
+$$
+\Spec(S) \longrightarrow \Spec(R)
+$$
+is a homeomorphism onto its image.
+\end{lemma}
+
+\begin{proof}
+The map is continuous by Lemma \ref{lemma-spec-functorial}. If
+$\mathfrak q$ and $\mathfrak q'$ have the same inverse image in $R$,
+then the assumption shows that every $g \in S$ is in $\mathfrak q$ if
+and only if it is in $\mathfrak q'$. Thus the map is injective. Finally,
+if $g = u\varphi(f)$ as in the statement, then
+$$
+D(g) = \Spec(\varphi)^{-1}(D(f)).
+$$
+Since the standard opens form a basis, the map is a homeomorphism onto
+its image.
+\end{proof}
